OS backend: report the system by name; scan only what LikeOS has.

smartctl -i and smartctl -V print the OS string of the backend, which
has the name of the system it was written for fixed into it.  On LikeOS
the name comes from uname(): machine-sysname-release.

smartctl --scan and smartd's DEVICESCAN look for /dev/hd[a-t], /dev/sd*
(and /dev/disk/by-id with -d by-id) and NVMe nodes, which is the LikeOS
naming as well, and then probe for MegaRAID and 3SNIC RAID controllers
through /proc/devices, /sys/class/scsi_host and /dev/bsg nodes.  LikeOS has
none of those, and the 3SNIC probe falls back to trying /dev/bsg/sssraid0
.. 16 and printing an "open ... error" line for each; so the two RAID
probes are left out of the scan.  Opening such a device by name with
-d megaraid,N or -d sssraid,N is unchanged and fails cleanly.

